Subject: DXVK dxso: no depth-compare sampler variant at the same binding
Date: 2026-10-24
Applies to: sources/dxvk (DXVK 1.10.3 cxaddon), after 0001
Files changed: src/dxso/dxso_compiler.cpp

For each sampler, DXVK's Direct3D 9 shader compiler declares a colour image
and a depth-compare ("shadow") image at the same binding and picks one with
a spec constant. MoltenVK 1.4.2 cannot translate that: with Metal argument
buffers SPIRV-Cross drops the shadow variant's sampler ("use of undeclared
identifier 's0_2d_shadowSmplr'"), and without them Metal rejects two
textures at one index ("cannot reserve 'texture' resource location"). In
Black Ops the screen stayed black: 42 and then 172 pixel shaders failed.

The depth-compare variant is no longer declared, and sampling always takes
the colour path. Hardware shadow-map comparisons then return the depth
value instead of a comparison result; Black Ops is played with shadows off
(sm_enable 0).
---
--- a/src/dxso/dxso_compiler.cpp
+++ b/src/dxso/dxso_compiler.cpp
@@ -826,10 +826,9 @@
 
       DclSampler(idx, binding, samplerType, false, implicit);
 
-      if (samplerType != SamplerTypeTexture3D) {
-        // We could also be depth compared!
-        DclSampler(idx, binding, samplerType, true, implicit);
-      }
+      // A depth-compare variant at the same binding cannot be translated by
+      // MoltenVK (one texture slot per binding in Metal), so it is not
+      // declared: depth textures are sampled like colour ones.
     }
     else {
       // Could be any of these!
@@ -838,9 +837,6 @@
         auto samplerType = static_cast<DxsoSamplerType>(i);
 
         DclSampler(idx, binding, samplerType, false, implicit);
-
-        if (samplerType != SamplerTypeTexture3D)
-          DclSampler(idx, binding, samplerType, true, implicit);
       }
     }
 
@@ -3054,8 +3050,9 @@
 
     auto SampleType = [&](DxsoSamplerType samplerType) {
       // Only do the check for depth comp. samplers
-      // if we aren't a 3D texture
-      if (samplerType != SamplerTypeTexture3D) {
+      // if we aren't a 3D texture, and only if the depth variant exists
+      // (it is not declared, see emitDclSampler).
+      if (samplerType != SamplerTypeTexture3D && sampler.depth[samplerType].varId) {
         uint32_t colorLabel  = m_module.allocateId();
         uint32_t depthLabel  = m_module.allocateId();
         uint32_t endLabel    = m_module.allocateId();
